    ("April 17", "Kateri Tekakwitha", A, "Mohawk-Algonquin woman (1656-1680), baptised in 1676, who endured hardship for her faith and became a model of prayer. She is honoured by Anglicans and Catholics.", "Native Americans, those who face rejection"),
