    ("May 29", "Juraj Tranovsky", P, "Slovak Lutheran pastor and hymn writer (1592-1637), often called the 'Luther of the Slavs', whose hymnal 'Cithara Sanctorum' remains in use.", "Hymn writers, Slovakia"),
    ("May 30", "Joan of Arc", PA, "French peasant girl (c. 1412-1431) who, guided by what she believed were heavenly voices, helped lead France's army and was executed for heresy. Rehabilitated by the Church, she is honoured by many traditions.", "France, soldiers, those unjustly condemned"),

    ("June 2", "Blandina and the Martyrs of Lyons", A, "A slave woman who with many other Christians was tortured and killed in Lyons in 177. Her courage strengthened the other martyrs.", "The persecuted, slaves"),
